To find the probability that exactly 4 of the 7 islands contain treasure, we use the binomial distribution.

\[
P(X=4)=\binom{7}{4}\left(\frac{1}{5}\right)^4\left(\frac{4}{5}\right)^{7-4}
\]

Calculate each part:

- \(\displaystyle \binom{7}{4}=35\)
- \(\displaystyle \left(\frac{1}{5}\right)^4=\frac{1}{625}\)
- \(\displaystyle \left(\frac{4}{5}\right)^3=\frac{64}{125}\)

Multiply them:

\[
P(X=4)=35 \times \frac{1}{625} \times \frac{64}{125}
      = \frac{35 \times 64}{625 \times 125}
      = \frac{2240}{78125}
      = \frac{448}{15625}
\]

\[
\boxed{\frac{448}{15625}}
\]

Answer: 448/15625
